Firmware formats
----------------
The ELE3 container, the SysEx transport and the packing format were first
documented by elektron-firmware-tool
(https://github.com/mischa85/elektron-firmware-tool, MIT, (c) 2026 Marcel
Bierling). No code from that tool is included; it served as a
cross-check.

octabam
-------
Facts about the Octatrack come from sambanks/octabam
(https://github.com/sambanks/octabam, MIT, (c) 2026 Sam Banks), and are
marked "octabam" where they are used (elekloader/devices/octatrack.py).
mods/core-ot makes the same 28 arena writes as octabam's platform, for the
same reservation. elekloader/sdk/octabam.py reads octabam's module manifests
from a checkout the user supplies, and copies their sources into the mod
folders it writes, with octabam's licence beside them. No octabam code is
included here.

Elektron
--------
Elektron, Digitakt, Digitone, Syntakt and Analog are trademarks of Elektron
Music Machines. elekloader is not affiliated with or endorsed by Elektron.
It contains no Elektron firmware and distributes nothing derived from it:
every build happens on the user's machine, from the stock OS file the user
supplies. Mods carry only their authors' own bytes, plus short instruction
fragments needed to hook the OS (runs of stock bytes under 8 bytes long, and
the instructions a hook displaces, are stored as they are), and hashes of
the stock bytes they expect.
